1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,940
A winery is a place that makes wine.

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,000
Some wineries also have a tasting room.

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:09,060
Visitors come to see the place, ask questions, and buy bottles.

4
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:11,980
A vineyard has grape plants.

5
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:14,260
Grapes are small fruit for wine.

6
00:00:15,360 --> 00:00:18,520
In the morning, workers may walk outside and check the plants.

7
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:22,620
They look for dry leaves, broken signs, or things that need care.

8
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:27,200
Inside the winery, there are bottles, boxes, shelves, and tools.

9
00:00:27,880 --> 00:00:29,900
Workers keep the area clean and safe.

10
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,160
A clean workplace helps visitors feel welcome.

11
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,480
One duty is checking bottles.

12
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:39,640
Workers may check the label, the box, and the number of bottles.

13
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,040
If one label is not straight, they fix it.

14
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,880
Visitors may ask simple questions.

15
00:00:46,660 --> 00:00:49,120
They may ask, "Where is the tasting room?

16
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,920
" or "Can I buy this bottle?

17
00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:56,080
" A worker can answer slowly and point to the place.

18
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,680
At the end of the day, workers clean the tasting room.

19
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:03,680
They wash glasses, put bottles back, and close the door.

20
00:01:04,580 --> 00:01:06,720
They also write a short note for the next day.

21
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:11,360
A visitor asks a winery worker about the workplace and daily duties.

22
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:13,420
Hello.

23
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:15,420
Do you work here?

24
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:17,660
Yes.

25
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:19,020
I work at this winery.

26
00:01:20,060 --> 00:01:21,620
What do you do every day?

27
00:01:22,980 --> 00:01:24,760
I check the grape plants in the morning.

28
00:01:26,120 --> 00:01:27,200
What do you do inside?

29
00:01:28,460 --> 00:01:30,020
I check bottles and labels.

30
00:01:31,180 --> 00:01:32,780
Is this the tasting room?

31
00:01:33,880 --> 00:01:34,580
Yes.

32
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:36,020
This is our tasting room.

33
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:38,420
Can I buy this bottle?

34
00:01:40,260 --> 00:01:40,960
Yes.

35
00:01:40,980 --> 00:01:42,420
You can buy it at the counter.

36
00:01:43,480 --> 00:01:45,360
What do you do at closing time?

37
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:49,100
I wash glasses and put bottles back.
